WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.083 --> 00:00:03.378
Do you think you’ve lost by 
being born black in a white country?

00:00:03.378 --> 00:00:04.212
No.

00:00:04.212 --> 00:00:05.630
I don’t look at it that way.

00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:08.800
The greatest influence

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:10.176
 in jazz of all time,

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:11.553
Louis Armstrong.

00:00:12.053 --> 00:00:13.304
♫ Cold empty bed. ♫ 

00:00:13.304 --> 00:00:16.266
Jazz almost stems 
from Louis Armstrong.

00:00:16.266 --> 00:00:18.518
♫ Wished I was dead. ♫ 

00:00:19.477 --> 00:00:20.645
♫ What did I do ♫ 

00:00:20.645 --> 00:00:23.898
Anybody who has uttered 
a sound on American radio.

00:00:23.898 --> 00:00:25.316
♫ To be so black and blue?♫ 

00:00:25.316 --> 00:00:28.361
It’s because of 
Louis Armstrong’s innovations.

00:00:29.571 --> 00:00:32.699
♫ scatting ♫ 

00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:36.244
He never would come out publicly,
 but at home he had his opinions.

00:00:37.495 --> 00:00:39.581
I’ve heard recordings 
of Pops just talking.  

00:00:40.248 --> 00:00:42.834
He understood there 
was a battle in this country.

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:51.301
There’s a rumor that
 you invented scat sing.

00:00:51.301 --> 00:00:53.219
It came to me just like that.

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:55.138
♫ scatting ♫ 

00:00:56.681 --> 00:00:58.683
To be black in those days,

00:00:58.683 --> 00:01:00.852
the discrimination 
was unbelievable.

00:01:01.853 --> 00:01:03.021
♫ Be so ♫ 

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:05.106
His own inner dignity

00:01:05.106 --> 00:01:06.858
was able to make him prevail

00:01:08.026 --> 00:01:10.487
over all these awful
conditions he worked with.

00:01:11.112 --> 00:01:12.280
♫ What did I do ♫ 

00:01:13.615 --> 00:01:15.867
He was the first 
black movie 

00:01:15.867 --> 00:01:19.120
performer to have his 
name above the title.

00:01:19.704 --> 00:01:20.789
♫ I do ♫ 

00:01:20.955 --> 00:01:23.166
He was trying to use 
his music to reform 

00:01:23.166 --> 00:01:26.169
and lead the country closer
 to his higher ideals.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:28.713
Arkansas has decided to make 

00:01:28.713 --> 00:01:30.632
its own laws on the 
subject of integration.

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:33.426
Louis said Ike and the 
government could go to hell.  

00:01:34.052 --> 00:01:35.261
Everybody was astonished,

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:39.349
but privately he expressed 
stuff like that all his life.

00:01:39.808 --> 00:01:40.975
♫ My only sin ♫ 

00:01:41.476 --> 00:01:42.685
All over the world.

00:01:42.685 --> 00:01:45.271
♫ is in my skin ♫

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:46.189
He had the respect.

00:01:46.189 --> 00:01:47.398
♫ They laugh at you ♫

00:01:47.398 --> 00:01:49.025
And the love of millions.

00:01:49.025 --> 00:01:51.986
♫ and scorn you too. ♫

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:53.863
♫ What did I do ♫

00:01:54.197 --> 00:01:55.698
What more can any 
man ask for?

00:01:56.074 --> 00:01:59.786
♫ to be so black and blue?♫

00:01:59.953 --> 00:02:01.830
Yeahhhhh.

